# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use Qiskit and IBM Quantum Compute Service developer tools to profile, customize, and inspect your experiment settings and runtime environment."
msgstr "Gamitin ang mga developer tool ng Qiskit at IBM Quantum Compute Service para mag-profile, mag-customize, at mag-inspect ng mga setting ng experiment at runtime environment mo."

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tools to profile, customize, and inspect experiments"
msgstr "Mga tool para mag-profile, mag-customize, at mag-inspect ng mga experiment"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"tutorials/profiling-tools.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Usage estimate: 10 minutes on a Heron r2 processor (NOTE: This is an estimate only. Your runtime might vary.)*\n"
msgstr "*Tantiya ng paggamit: 10 minuto sa isang Heron r2 processor (PAALALA: Tantiya lang ito. Maaaring iba ang runtime mo.)*\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To get good results from a quantum computer, you need more than a well-designed circuit. The device's current condition, how your circuit is scheduled, the noise that the circuit experiences, and when and how your job runs on the quantum processing unit (QPU) all affect the quality of your results. Qiskit and IBM Quantum&reg; Compute Service offer a growing set of developer tools that expose this information. You can use these tools to act on that information before you commit QPU time to a full experiment, and to debug a finished experiment.\n"
msgstr "Para makakuha ng magagandang resulta mula sa quantum computer, kailangan mo ng higit pa sa isang mahusay na dinisenyong circuit. Nakakaapekto sa kalidad ng mga resulta mo ang kasalukuyang kondisyon ng device, kung paano naka-schedule ang circuit mo, ang noise na nararanasan ng circuit, at kung kailan at paano tumatakbo ang job mo sa quantum processing unit (QPU). Nag-aalok ang Qiskit at IBM Quantum&reg; Compute Service ng lumalaking hanay ng mga developer tool na naglalantad ng impormasyong ito. Magagamit mo ang mga tool na ito para kumilos ayon sa impormasyong iyon bago ka gumugol ng QPU time sa buong experiment, at para mag-debug ng natapos na experiment.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial uses a single end-to-end experiment to show how to combine these tools at each stage of a typical development workflow. Not every tool is useful for every experiment, so choose the tools that address the questions that you have about your own workload.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang tutorial na ito ng isang end-to-end na experiment para ipakita kung paano pagsamahin ang mga tool na ito sa bawat yugto ng karaniwang development workflow. Hindi kapaki-pakinabang ang bawat tool sa bawat experiment, kaya piliin ang mga tool na sumasagot sa mga tanong mo tungkol sa sarili mong workload.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow is as follows:\n"
msgstr "Ang workflow ay ang sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare a mirror circuit of a Trotterized time evolution of a linear transverse-field Ising model.\n"
msgstr "Maghanda ng mirror circuit ng Trotterized na time evolution ng isang linear na transverse-field Ising model.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select a backend with an alternative calibration data set that is designed for error mitigation methods based on a noise model.\n"
msgstr "Pumili ng backend na may alternatibong calibration data set na dinisenyo para sa mga error mitigation method na nakabatay sa noise model.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run device benchmarking experiments so that the transpiler uses up-to-date device properties when it selects a layout.\n"
msgstr "Magpatakbo ng mga device benchmarking experiment para gumamit ang transpiler ng napapanahong mga property ng device kapag pumipili ito ng layout.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect the timing information of the scheduled circuit.\n"
msgstr "Suriin ang timing information ng na-schedule na circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn Pauli-Lindblad and readout noise models for the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Alamin ang mga Pauli-Lindblad at readout noise model para sa circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run noiseless, unmitigated, and mitigated local simulations. The noisy simulations use the learned noise model to show how much improvement you might gain from the selected error mitigation methods. This tutorial uses probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) and Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX).\n"
msgstr "Magpatakbo ng mga noiseless, unmitigated, at mitigated na lokal na simulation. Ginagamit ng mga noisy na simulation ang natutunang noise model para ipakita kung gaano kalaking pagbuti ang maaari mong makuha mula sa mga napiling error mitigation method. Gumagamit ang tutorial na ito ng probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) at Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '7. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get a usage estimate without running on a QPU, to check whether you need to adjust the experiment to fit your budget.\n"
msgstr "Kumuha ng tantiya ng paggamit nang hindi tumatakbo sa QPU, para tingnan kung kailangan mong ayusin ang experiment para magkasya sa budget mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '8. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Start a session and trigger calibration so that the experiment uses the most recent calibration data.\n"
msgstr "Magsimula ng session at mag-trigger ng calibration para gamitin ng experiment ang pinakabagong calibration data.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '9. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the experiment on the QPU by using Estimator, and compare the hardware results with the simulated preview.\n"
msgstr "Patakbuhin ang experiment sa QPU gamit ang Estimator, at ihambing ang mga resulta ng hardware sa simulated na preview.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '10. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect the execution spans to see whether there are significant gaps between groups of executions (chunks).\n"
msgstr "Suriin ang mga execution span para makita kung may malalaking puwang sa pagitan ng mga grupo ng execution (mga chunk).\n"

