# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Specify a circuit and observable {#step-1-specify-a-circuit-and-observable}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1: Tukuyin ang circuit at observable {#step-1-specify-a-circuit-and-observable}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare a mirror circuit of a Trotterized time evolution of a linear transverse-field Ising model. Mirror the circuit to cancel the circuit unitary and form an identity circuit. Because the ideal output is the all-zero state, the ideal expectation value of each single-qubit $Z$ observable is 1. Mirroring also doubles the circuit depth, which amplifies the effect of noise.\n"
msgstr "Maghanda ng mirror circuit ng Trotterized na time evolution ng isang linear na transverse-field Ising model. I-mirror ang circuit para kanselahin ang unitary ng circuit at makabuo ng identity circuit. Dahil ang ideal na output ay ang all-zero na state, 1 ang ideal na expectation value ng bawat single-qubit na $Z$ observable. Dinodoble rin ng mirroring ang lalim ng circuit, na nagpapalakas sa epekto ng noise.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/profiling-tools/extracted-outputs/caa280da-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/profiling-tools/extracted-outputs/caa280da-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2: I-optimize para sa pagpapatakbo sa quantum hardware {#step-2-optimize-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.1 Use alternative calibration if applicable {#21-use-alternative-calibration-if-applicable}"
msgstr "2.1 Gumamit ng alternatibong calibration kung naaangkop {#21-use-alternative-calibration-if-applicable}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM&reg; calibrates its QPUs periodically for good performance across general use cases. Some workloads, however, benefit from instructions whose parameters are tuned differently. For more information, refer to [Specially calibrated instructions](/guides/custom-calibration).\n"
msgstr "Pana-panahong kina-calibrate ng IBM&reg; ang mga QPU nito para sa mahusay na performance sa pangkalahatang mga use case. Gayunman, may mga workload na nakikinabang sa mga instruction na iba ang pagkaka-tune ng mga parameter. Para sa higit pang impormasyon, tingnan ang [Mga espesyal na na-calibrate na instruction](/guides/custom-calibration).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial uses an alternative calibration data set called `slow_gates_ac`. This calibration contains a slower `cz` gate and modulates the two-level system (TLS) bias to stabilize device errors over time. These changes benefit error mitigation methods that rely on a learned noise model. The `slow_gates_ac` calibration is available only on Heron QPUs. If you run on a Nighthawk QPU, use `slow_gates` instead.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang tutorial na ito ng alternatibong calibration data set na tinatawag na `slow_gates_ac`. May mas mabagal na `cz` gate ang calibration na ito at minomodulate nito ang two-level system (TLS) bias para patatagin ang mga error ng device sa paglipas ng panahon. Nakikinabang dito ang mga error mitigation method na umaasa sa natutunang noise model. Available lang ang `slow_gates_ac` calibration sa mga Heron QPU. Kung tatakbo ka sa Nighthawk QPU, gamitin na lang ang `slow_gates`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.2 Run real-time device benchmarking {#22-run-real-time-device-benchmarking}"
msgstr "2.2 Magpatakbo ng real-time na device benchmarking {#22-run-real-time-device-benchmarking}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One of the most critical stages of transpilation is layout selection, which maps virtual qubits in a circuit to physical qubits on the target device. A good layout minimizes the number of SWAP operations needed and places the circuit on the best-performing qubits, so the quality of the initial layout can significantly affect the quality of your results.\n"
msgstr "Isa sa pinakakritikal na yugto ng transpilation ang pagpili ng layout, na nagma-map ng mga virtual na qubit sa isang circuit papunta sa mga pisikal na qubit sa target na device. Binabawasan ng magandang layout ang bilang ng mga SWAP operation na kailangan at inilalagay ang circuit sa mga qubit na pinakamahusay ang performance, kaya ang kalidad ng paunang layout ay malaki ang epekto sa kalidad ng mga resulta mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Periodic benchmarking routines run on every IBM QPU to report the current performance of its qubits: relaxation times ($T_1$), coherence times ($T_2$), readout errors, and one- and two-qubit gate errors. The Qiskit transpiler uses these metrics during layout selection.\n"
msgstr "May mga pana-panahong benchmarking routine na tumatakbo sa bawat IBM QPU para iulat ang kasalukuyang performance ng mga qubit nito: mga relaxation time ($T_1$), mga coherence time ($T_2$), mga readout error, at mga error ng one- at two-qubit gate. Ginagamit ng Qiskit transpiler ang mga metric na ito sa pagpili ng layout.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The properties of superconducting qubits, however, can drift on shorter timescales, and transient defects, known as TLSs, can temporarily degrade a qubit that performed well at calibration time. If the transpiler uses outdated information, it cannot select the best layout. Therefore, it can be worthwhile to spend some QPU time to characterize the device before you select a layout.\n"
msgstr "Gayunman, ang mga property ng superconducting na qubit ay maaaring mag-drift sa mas maiikling timescale, at ang mga pansamantalang depekto, na kilala bilang mga TLS, ay maaaring pansamantalang magpababa sa isang qubit na maganda ang performance noong oras ng calibration. Kung gumagamit ang transpiler ng lumang impormasyon, hindi nito mapipili ang pinakamahusay na layout. Kaya maaaring sulit na gumugol ng kaunting QPU time para i-characterize ang device bago ka pumili ng layout.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Refer to the [Refresh backend properties with real-time benchmarking](/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking) tutorial for a detailed walk-through.\n"
"The characterization suite builds several experiments, submits multiple jobs, and fits the results. This process can take a few minutes in total. Enable INFO-level logging so that each stage prints its progress as it runs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tingnan ang tutorial na [Refresh backend properties with real-time benchmarking](/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking) para sa detalyadong walk-through.\n"
"Bumubuo ang characterization suite ng ilang experiment, nagsusumite ng maraming job, at nagfi-fit ng mga resulta. Maaaring tumagal nang ilang minuto ang prosesong ito sa kabuuan. I-enable ang INFO-level na logging para mag-print ang bawat yugto ng progreso nito habang tumatakbo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`BackendCharacterization` is a convenience class that runs the characterization experiments of your choice, analyzes the results, and returns an updated `Backend` object that you can pass to the transpiler.\n"
msgstr "Ang `BackendCharacterization` ay isang convenience class na nagpapatakbo ng mga characterization experiment na pinili mo, nag-aanalisa ng mga resulta, at nagbabalik ng na-update na `Backend` object na maaari mong ipasa sa transpiler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You might see a warning that a backend was passed in as the mode while a batch is open. This warning is expected, and you can safely ignore it.\n"
msgstr "Maaari kang makakita ng babala na may backend na ipinasa bilang mode habang bukas ang isang batch. Inaasahan ang babalang ito, at ligtas mo itong balewalain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.3 Transpile to ISA {#23-transpile-to-isa}"
msgstr "2.3 I-transpile sa ISA {#23-transpile-to-isa}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transform the circuit and observables to match the backend's instruction set architecture (ISA) by using the refreshed device properties.\n"
msgstr "Baguhin ang circuit at mga observable para tumugma sa instruction set architecture (ISA) ng backend gamit ang na-refresh na mga property ng device.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.4 Visualize circuit timing {#24-visualize-circuit-timing}"
msgstr "2.4 I-visualize ang circuit timing {#24-visualize-circuit-timing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to the instructions in a circuit, you might want to visualize the circuit's schedule, to find idle time on qubits or inefficient instruction alignment. You can get the most detailed and accurate timing information from IBM Quantum Compute Service by using dry-run mode.\n"
msgstr "Bukod sa mga instruction sa isang circuit, baka gusto mo ring i-visualize ang schedule ng circuit, para makita ang idle time sa mga qubit o hindi episyenteng alignment ng mga instruction. Makukuha mo ang pinakadetalyado at pinakatumpak na timing information mula sa IBM Quantum Compute Service sa pamamagitan ng dry-run mode.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit in this tutorial is static, so its schedule is not very informative. You can get similar timing information locally from the circuit and the backend properties, for example by using the [timeline drawer](/guides/visualize-circuit-timing) built into Qiskit. This tutorial includes this step to show how to request and visualize the timing information. Timing information from the service is most useful for [dynamic circuits](/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow). Dynamic circuits contain mid-circuit measurements, conditional operations, and feedforward, which add implicit operations such as broadcasting measurement results and determining branches. The timing of these operations cannot be determined from the circuit and backend properties alone.\n"
msgstr "Static ang circuit sa tutorial na ito, kaya hindi masyadong informative ang schedule nito. Makakakuha ka ng katulad na timing information nang lokal mula sa circuit at sa mga property ng backend, halimbawa gamit ang [timeline drawer](/guides/visualize-circuit-timing) na built-in sa Qiskit. Kasama sa tutorial na ito ang hakbang na ito para ipakita kung paano humiling at mag-visualize ng timing information. Pinakamakatulong ang timing information mula sa service para sa [dynamic circuits](/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow). May mid-circuit measurement, conditional operation, at feedforward ang mga dynamic circuit, na nagdaragdag ng mga implicit operation gaya ng pag-broadcast ng mga resulta ng measurement at pagtukoy ng mga branch. Hindi matutukoy ang timing ng mga operasyong ito mula lang sa circuit at mga property ng backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Refer to [Visualize circuit timing](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing) for more information.\n"
"Scheduled circuit timing is available only for Sampler and Executor jobs, so the following cell submits the circuit in dry-run mode by using Sampler. Jobs that you submit in dry-run mode do not run on real QPUs and are not charged.\n"
msgstr ""
