# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Apply error mitigation and test locally {#step-3-apply-error-mitigation-and-test-locally}"
msgstr "Step 3: Mag-apply ng error mitigation at mag-test nang lokal {#step-3-apply-error-mitigation-and-test-locally}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.1 Cliffordize the circuit {#31-cliffordize-the-circuit}"
msgstr "3.1 I-Cliffordize ang circuit {#31-cliffordize-the-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The cost of general noisy simulation grows exponentially with the number of qubits, and most laptops cannot simulate more than about 32 qubits. Therefore, first convert the circuit to a Clifford circuit, which a stabilizer simulator can handle far more efficiently. The conversion rounds each rotation angle to a Clifford angle, so the simulated circuit approximates the original circuit rather than reproducing it.\n"
msgstr "Exponential ang pagtaas ng gastos ng pangkalahatang noisy simulation kasabay ng bilang ng mga qubit, at karamihan sa mga laptop ay hindi kayang mag-simulate ng higit sa humigit-kumulang 32 qubit. Kaya, i-convert muna ang circuit sa isang Clifford circuit, na mas episyenteng mahahawakan ng isang stabilizer simulator. Ni-round ng conversion ang bawat rotation angle sa isang Clifford angle, kaya ang na-simulate na circuit ay tinatantiya lang ang orihinal na circuit at hindi ito eksaktong ginagaya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.2 Apply PEC with TREX {#32-apply-pec-with-trex}"
msgstr "3.2 Mag-apply ng PEC gamit ang TREX {#32-apply-pec-with-trex}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It can be difficult to select error mitigation methods that balance cost and accuracy for your specific experiment. You can use the `select-error-mitigation` AI agent skill to analyze the available methods for your workload. The skill presents a summary report that explains whether each method was selected and why.\n"
msgstr "Mahirap minsang pumili ng mga error mitigation method na nagbabalanse ng gastos at katumpakan para sa partikular mong experiment. Magagamit mo ang `select-error-mitigation` AI agent skill para suriin ang mga available na method para sa workload mo. Nagpapakita ang skill ng summary report na nagpapaliwanag kung napili ba ang bawat method at kung bakit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Refer to the [Qiskit AI skills](https://github.com/Qiskit/skills) GitHub repository for more information.\n"
"This tutorial uses PEC with TREX directly, so that you can complete it without an AI agent.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tingnan ang [Qiskit AI skills](https://github.com/Qiskit/skills) GitHub repository para sa karagdagang impormasyon.\n"
"Direktang ginagamit ng tutorial na ito ang PEC kasama ang TREX, para makumpleto mo ito nang walang AI agent.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC is a technique that mitigates quantum noise when you calculate the expectation values of observables. Under ideal conditions, PEC can produce an unbiased estimate of the expectation values. It learns the noise of each layer of two-qubit gates, then runs an ensemble of circuits that, on average, apply the inverse of that noise. PEC uses Pauli twirling to tailor the noise into a Pauli channel, which can be learned and inverted efficiently.\n"
msgstr "Ang PEC ay isang technique na nagbabawas ng quantum noise kapag kinakalkula mo ang mga expectation value ng mga observable. Sa ideal na kondisyon, makakabuo ang PEC ng unbiased na estimate ng mga expectation value. Natututunan nito ang noise ng bawat layer ng mga two-qubit gate, saka nagpapatakbo ng ensemble ng mga circuit na, sa average, nag-a-apply ng inverse ng noise na iyon. Gumagamit ang PEC ng Pauli twirling para gawing Pauli channel ang noise, na mabisang matututunan at ma-i-invert.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In practice, PEC is only as accurate as the learned noise model. The sparse Pauli-Lindblad model includes only one- and two-qubit error terms on neighboring qubits, and it cannot fully capture effects such as crosstalk between distant qubits or time-correlated errors. The device noise can also drift between noise learning and execution. PEC does not cancel noise that the model misses, and it overcompensates for noise that the model overestimates. Therefore, mitigated results can still deviate from the ideal values in either direction.\n"
msgstr "Sa praktika, kasing-tumpak lang ng natutunang noise model ang PEC. Ang sparse Pauli-Lindblad model ay may kasamang one- at two-qubit error term lang sa mga magkatabing qubit, at hindi nito lubos na nakukuha ang mga epekto gaya ng crosstalk sa pagitan ng mga malalayong qubit o mga time-correlated na error. Maaari ring mag-drift ang noise ng device sa pagitan ng noise learning at execution. Hindi kinakansela ng PEC ang noise na hindi nakuha ng model, at sobra ang kompensasyon nito sa noise na sobra ang pagtantiya ng model. Kaya, maaari pa ring lumihis ang mga mitigated na resulta mula sa mga ideal na value sa alinmang direksyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"TREX is a technique that mitigates measurement errors, and is useful when you estimate the expectation values of Pauli observables. It relies on measurement twirling, which diagonalizes the readout-error transfer matrix and makes it easy to invert. TREX learns a rescaling term from the diagonal noise channel by measuring twirled calibration circuits that are initialized in the zero state.\n"
"You can enable both PEC and TREX by setting Estimator options. This tutorial uses the client-side implementations of the Qiskit SamplerV2 and EstimatorV2 interfaces, which were introduced in `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0. These client-side primitives perform most of the pre- and post-processing locally and delegate execution to the Executor primitive. When the primitives run on the client side, you get greater transparency, faster feedback when you debug, and finer control.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang TREX ay isang technique na nagbabawas ng mga measurement error, at kapaki-pakinabang kapag tinatantiya mo ang mga expectation value ng mga Pauli observable. Umaasa ito sa measurement twirling, na nagdi-diagonalize sa readout-error transfer matrix at ginagawa itong madaling i-invert. Natututunan ng TREX ang isang rescaling term mula sa diagonal noise channel sa pamamagitan ng pag-measure ng mga twirled calibration circuit na naka-initialize sa zero state.\n"
"Maaari mong i-enable ang PEC at TREX nang sabay sa pamamagitan ng pagtatakda ng mga Estimator option. Ginagamit ng tutorial na ito ang mga client-side implementation ng mga interface na Qiskit SamplerV2 at EstimatorV2, na ipinakilala sa `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0. Ginagawa ng mga client-side primitive na ito ang karamihan ng pre- at post-processing nang lokal at ipinapasa ang execution sa Executor primitive. Kapag tumatakbo ang mga primitive sa client side, mas malinaw ang nangyayari, mas mabilis ang feedback kapag nagde-debug, at mas pino ang kontrol.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The client-side primitives implement the same API as the legacy server-side primitives. Therefore, you can usually switch to the client-side primitives by changing only the import statement.\n"
"Enable INFO-level logging to see the progress of client-side pre- and post-processing.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinapatupad ng mga client-side primitive ang parehong API ng mga legacy na server-side primitive. Kaya, kadalasan ay makakalipat ka sa mga client-side primitive sa pamamagitan lang ng pagbabago ng import statement.\n"
"I-enable ang INFO-level logging para makita ang progress ng client-side pre- at post-processing.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.3 Learn noise models and run the Cliffordized circuit {#33-learn-noise-models-and-run-the-cliffordized-circuit}"
msgstr "3.3 Matuto ng mga noise model at patakbuhin ang Cliffordized na circuit {#33-learn-noise-models-and-run-the-cliffordized-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both PEC and TREX require noise learning, which you can do with `NoiseLearnerV3`. The steps are as follows:\n"
msgstr "Kailangan ng noise learning ng parehong PEC at TREX, na magagawa mo gamit ang `NoiseLearnerV3`. Ang mga hakbang ay ang sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find the unique two-qubit gate layers and measurement layers in the circuit, for the Pauli-Lindblad and TREX protocols, respectively.\n"
msgstr "Hanapin ang mga natatanging two-qubit gate layer at measurement layer sa circuit, para sa mga Pauli-Lindblad at TREX protocol, ayon sa pagkakasunod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass the layers to `NoiseLearnerV3` to learn the noise models.\n"
msgstr "Ipasa ang mga layer sa `NoiseLearnerV3` para matutunan ang mga noise model.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Convert the learned noise models to Pauli-Lindblad maps.\n"
msgstr "I-convert ang mga natutunang noise model sa mga Pauli-Lindblad map.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Estimator does not use a pre-learned TREX noise model. Instead, it performs its own TREX learning. The following code learns both models anyway, because the noisy simulation uses the learned readout model.\n"
msgstr "Hindi gumagamit ang Estimator ng pre-learned na TREX noise model. Sa halip, gumagawa ito ng sarili nitong TREX learning. Natututunan pa rin ng sumusunod na code ang dalawang model, dahil ginagamit ng noisy simulation ang natutunang readout model.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Refer to [Noise learning helper](/guides/noise-learning) for more information about `NoiseLearnerV3`.\n"
"In addition to the noise-learning experiment, run the Cliffordized circuit on the QPU. This step is not always necessary, but it provides a comparison for the simulated results in Step 3.4.4. Run both in a batch to minimize how much the noise profile drifts between the two.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tingnan ang [Noise learning helper](/guides/noise-learning) para sa karagdagang impormasyon tungkol sa `NoiseLearnerV3`.\n"
"Bukod sa noise-learning experiment, patakbuhin ang Cliffordized na circuit sa QPU. Hindi laging kailangan ang hakbang na ito, pero nagbibigay ito ng paghahambing para sa mga na-simulate na resulta sa Step 3.4.4. Patakbuhin ang dalawa sa isang batch para mabawasan ang pag-drift ng noise profile sa pagitan nila.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.4 Perform local simulation {#34-perform-local-simulation}"
msgstr "3.4 Magsagawa ng lokal na simulation {#34-perform-local-simulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With `qiskit-ibm-runtime` local mode, you can perform both noiseless and noisy simulations locally with minimal code changes. Use local mode to verify syntactic correctness, compare the effects of different mitigation methods, and check how well the learned noise model agrees with hardware results.\n"
msgstr "Sa local mode ng `qiskit-ibm-runtime`, makakapagsagawa ka ng parehong noiseless at noisy na simulation nang lokal na may kaunting pagbabago lang sa code. Gamitin ang local mode para i-verify ang syntactic correctness, ihambing ang mga epekto ng iba't ibang mitigation method, at suriin kung gaano katugma ang natutunang noise model sa mga resulta ng hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Local mode uses largely the same interface as QPU execution. In most cases, you need to change only the backend that you pass when you initialize the primitive, and then rerun the same code. Each of the following subsections creates its own `Estimator` instance, so you can run them without changing a previous cell.\n"
msgstr "Halos pareho ang interface ng local mode sa QPU execution. Sa karamihan ng kaso, kailangan mo lang palitan ang backend na ipinapasa mo kapag ini-initialize ang primitive, at pagkatapos ay patakbuhin ulit ang parehong code. Gumagawa ang bawat isa sa mga sumusunod na subsection ng sarili nitong `Estimator` instance, kaya mapapatakbo mo ang mga ito nang hindi binabago ang naunang cell.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Refer to [Local mode](/guides/local-testing-mode) for more information.\n"
msgstr "Tingnan ang [Local mode](/guides/local-testing-mode) para sa karagdagang impormasyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.4.1 Run a noiseless simulation {#341-run-a-noiseless-simulation}"
msgstr "3.4.1 Magpatakbo ng noiseless na simulation {#341-run-a-noiseless-simulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.4.2 Run a noisy simulation with the learned Pauli-Lindblad model {#342-run-a-noisy-simulation-with-the-learned-pauli-lindblad-model}"
msgstr "3.4.2 Magpatakbo ng noisy na simulation gamit ang natutunang Pauli-Lindblad model {#342-run-a-noisy-simulation-with-the-learned-pauli-lindblad-model}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
