#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Do not use a fake backend or a Qiskit Aer noise model if you plan to use the learned Pauli-Lindblad noise model in your local simulation. If you do, the simulation applies the noise twice.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Huwag gumamit ng fake backend o Qiskit Aer noise model kung plano mong gamitin ang natutunang Pauli-Lindblad noise model sa lokal mong simulation. Kung gagawin mo iyon, dalawang beses ia-apply ng simulation ang noise.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.4.3 Run a noisy simulation with PEC and TREX {#343-run-a-noisy-simulation-with-pec-and-trex}"
msgstr "3.4.3 Magpatakbo ng noisy na simulation gamit ang PEC at TREX {#343-run-a-noisy-simulation-with-pec-and-trex}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.4.4 Compare the simulation results {#344-compare-the-simulation-results}"
msgstr "3.4.4 Ihambing ang mga resulta ng simulation {#344-compare-the-simulation-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore frameon sharey */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plot the expectation value of each single-qubit $Z$ observable from the three simulations, together with the unmitigated QPU result for the same Clifford circuit from Step 3.3. Because the circuit is a mirror circuit, every ideal value is 1. The error bars show the standard error that Estimator reports for each value.\n"
msgstr "I-plot ang expectation value ng bawat single-qubit na $Z$ observable mula sa tatlong simulation, kasama ang unmitigated na resulta ng QPU para sa parehong Clifford circuit mula sa Step 3.3. Dahil mirror circuit ang circuit, 1 ang bawat ideal na value. Ipinapakita ng mga error bar ang standard error na iniuulat ng Estimator para sa bawat value.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The closer the unmitigated simulation is to the unmitigated QPU result, the better the learned noise model describes the hardware. Use this comparison as a check before you spend QPU time on the mitigated experiment. If the two results disagree significantly, PEC is also unlikely to get close to the ideal values on hardware. In that case, consider relearning the noise model or selecting a different layout. You can also relearn the noise model with different `NoiseLearnerV3` options, such as more randomizations or additional layer-pair depths, and check whether the agreement improves. For example, in Step 3.3 this tutorial sets `num_randomizations` to 64 instead of the default value of 32, because the additional randomizations improved the agreement for this circuit.\n"
msgstr "Kapag mas malapit ang unmitigated na simulation sa unmitigated na resulta ng QPU, mas mahusay na inilalarawan ng natutunang noise model ang hardware. Gamitin ang paghahambing na ito bilang pagsusuri bago ka gumastos ng oras ng QPU sa mitigated na experiment. Kung malaki ang pagkakaiba ng dalawang resulta, malabong mapalapit din ang PEC sa mga ideal na value sa hardware. Sa ganitong kaso, isaalang-alang ang muling pag-learn ng noise model o pagpili ng ibang layout. Maaari mo ring muling i-learn ang noise model gamit ang iba't ibang option ng `NoiseLearnerV3`, gaya ng mas maraming randomization o karagdagang layer-pair depth, at tingnan kung gumaganda ang pagkakatugma. Halimbawa, sa Step 3.3, itinakda ng tutorial na ito ang `num_randomizations` sa 64 sa halip na sa default na value na 32, dahil pinaganda ng karagdagang randomization ang pagkakatugma para sa circuit na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`NoiseLearnerV3` runs a standard learning protocol. For full control over the learning experiment, you can build your own with [Qiskit noise learning](/addons/qiskit-noise-learning/guides/workflow).\n"
msgstr "Nagpapatakbo ang `NoiseLearnerV3` ng standard na learning protocol. Para sa buong kontrol sa learning experiment, makakagawa ka ng sarili mo gamit ang [Qiskit noise learning](/addons/qiskit-noise-learning/guides/workflow).\n"

