# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.5 Estimate usage {#35-estimate-usage}"
msgstr "3.5 Tantiyahin ang usage {#35-estimate-usage}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The main purpose of dry-run mode is to estimate usage. Unlike local mode, dry-run mode submits the job to IBM Quantum Compute Service, which returns an accurate usage estimate but **random result data**. Dry-run jobs do not run on real QPUs and do not consume any QPU time.\n"
msgstr "Ang pangunahing layunin ng dry-run mode ay tantiyahin ang usage. Hindi tulad ng local mode, isinusumite ng dry-run mode ang job sa IBM Quantum Compute Service, na nagbabalik ng tumpak na usage estimate pero **random na result data**. Hindi tumatakbo sa totoong QPU ang mga dry-run job at hindi gumagamit ng anumang oras ng QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dry-run jobs are not available on the Open or Pay-As-You-Go plans.\n"
msgstr "Hindi available ang mga dry-run job sa mga Open o Pay-As-You-Go plan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Refer to [Dry-run jobs](/guides/dry-run-jobs) for more information.\n"
msgstr "Tingnan ang [Dry-run jobs](/guides/dry-run-jobs) para sa karagdagang impormasyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Run on hardware {#step-4-run-on-hardware}"
msgstr "Step 4: Magpatakbo sa hardware {#step-4-run-on-hardware}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.1 Initialize a session and run calibration {#41-initialize-a-session-and-run-calibration}"
msgstr "4.1 Mag-initialize ng session at magpatakbo ng calibration {#41-initialize-a-session-and-run-calibration}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "QPU calibration optimizes many parameters that define the electrical signals that drive the quantum gates and operations. Calibration jobs run throughout the day between user jobs, but not during an active session. These parameters can drift within a short period of time. For the best possible results, consider triggering calibration at the start of a session, or periodically during a long-running session.\n"
msgstr "Ino-optimize ng QPU calibration ang maraming parameter na tumutukoy sa mga electrical signal na nagpapatakbo sa mga quantum gate at operasyon. Tumatakbo ang mga calibration job sa buong araw sa pagitan ng mga job ng user, pero hindi sa gitna ng aktibong session. Maaaring mag-drift ang mga parameter na ito sa maikling panahon. Para sa pinakamagandang posibleng resulta, isaalang-alang ang pag-trigger ng calibration sa simula ng session, o pana-panahon sa isang matagal na session.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Currently, only readout calibration is supported, and it takes approximately five minutes of wall-clock time.\n"
msgstr "Sa kasalukuyan, readout calibration lang ang suportado, at tumatagal ito ng humigit-kumulang limang minuto ng wall-clock time.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.2 Run on hardware with Estimator {#42-run-on-hardware-with-estimator}"
msgstr "4.2 Magpatakbo sa hardware gamit ang Estimator {#42-run-on-hardware-with-estimator}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following cells run three jobs in the batch or session:\n"
msgstr "Nagpapatakbo ang mga sumusunod na cell ng tatlong job sa batch o session:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A noise-learning experiment to refresh the noise model. This experiment is useful if you expect the noise model from Step 3.3 to be outdated when the Estimator job runs. In a batch, the Estimator jobs can run much later than the noise-learning job, because jobs from other users can run on the QPU between them. A session gives your workload exclusive access to the QPU, so the noise model is more likely to still be accurate when the experiment runs.\n"
msgstr "Isang noise-learning experiment para i-refresh ang noise model. Kapaki-pakinabang ang experiment na ito kung inaasahan mong luma na ang noise model mula sa Step 3.3 kapag tumakbo ang Estimator job. Sa isang batch, maaaring tumakbo nang mas huli ang mga Estimator job kaysa sa noise-learning job, dahil maaaring tumakbo sa QPU ang mga job ng ibang user sa pagitan ng mga ito. Binibigyan ng session ang workload mo ng eksklusibong access sa QPU, kaya mas malamang na tumpak pa rin ang noise model kapag tumakbo ang experiment.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The experiment with mitigation.\n"
msgstr "Ang experiment na may mitigation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The experiment without mitigation, for comparison.\n"
msgstr "Ang experiment na walang mitigation, para sa paghahambing.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plot the mitigated and unmitigated hardware results together with the ideal values. Because the circuit is a mirror circuit, every ideal value is 1, so the distance between each point and the dashed line shows the remaining error. Any remaining deviation from the ideal value, whether above or below it, reflects the statistical uncertainty of PEC and the limits of the learned noise model described in Step 3.2.\n"
msgstr "I-plot ang mga mitigated at unmitigated na resulta ng hardware kasama ang mga ideal na value. Dahil mirror circuit ang circuit, 1 ang bawat ideal na value, kaya ang distansya ng bawat punto sa dashed line ay nagpapakita ng natitirang error. Anumang natitirang paglihis mula sa ideal na value, sa itaas man o sa ibaba nito, ay sumasalamin sa statistical uncertainty ng PEC at sa mga limitasyon ng natutunang noise model na inilarawan sa Step 3.2.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To further improve the results, you can try the following:\n"
msgstr "Para mas mapabuti pa ang mga resulta, maaari mong subukan ang sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Increase the number of shots or randomizations to reduce the statistical uncertainty of the mitigated estimates. The cost grows with the PEC sampling overhead.\n"
msgstr "Dagdagan ang bilang ng mga shot o randomization para mabawasan ang statistical uncertainty ng mga mitigated na estimate. Tumataas ang gastos kasabay ng PEC sampling overhead.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Relearn the noise model immediately before the experiment, in the same session, to reduce the effect of noise drift.\n"
msgstr "Muling i-learn ang noise model bago mismo ang experiment, sa parehong session, para mabawasan ang epekto ng noise drift.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the noise model more precisely by increasing the `num_randomizations`, `shots_per_randomization`, or `layer_pair_depths` options of `NoiseLearnerV3`. Errors in the learned rates bias the mitigated results, and additional PEC shots do not remove this bias.\n"
msgstr "Mas tumpak na i-learn ang noise model sa pamamagitan ng pagtaas ng mga option na `num_randomizations`, `shots_per_randomization`, o `layer_pair_depths` ng `NoiseLearnerV3`. Nagdudulot ng bias sa mga mitigated na resulta ang mga error sa mga natutunang rate, at hindi ito natatanggal ng karagdagang PEC shot.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add [non-Markovian error checks](/addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/postselection-with-non-markovian-error-checks) to detect shots that are likely corrupted by non-Markovian errors, which the learned noise model does not describe. Then discard those shots by postselection. Apply the same checks when you learn the noise model, by using the `bit_flip_checks` options of `NoiseLearnerV3`. Otherwise, the learned model includes errors that postselection removes from the experiment, and PEC overcompensates for them. Stricter postselection discards more shots, so balance the accuracy gain against the number of shots that you keep.\n"
msgstr "Magdagdag ng [non-Markovian error checks](/addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/postselection-with-non-markovian-error-checks) para matukoy ang mga shot na malamang na sira dahil sa mga non-Markovian error, na hindi inilalarawan ng natutunang noise model. Pagkatapos ay itapon ang mga shot na iyon sa pamamagitan ng postselection. I-apply ang parehong mga check kapag nag-learn ka ng noise model, gamit ang mga option na `bit_flip_checks` ng `NoiseLearnerV3`. Kung hindi, kasama sa natutunang model ang mga error na inaalis ng postselection sa experiment, at sobra ang kompensasyon ng PEC para sa mga iyon. Mas maraming shot ang itinatapon ng mas mahigpit na postselection, kaya balansehin ang pagbuti ng katumpakan laban sa bilang ng mga shot na pinapanatili mo.\n"

