msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/profiling-tools/extracted-outputs/3cd8d65c-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.3 Compare hardware and simulation results {#43-compare-hardware-and-simulation-results}"
msgstr "4.3 Ihambing ang mga resulta ng hardware at simulation {#43-compare-hardware-and-simulation-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In Step 3.4, you used local simulation to preview how much PEC and TREX might improve the results. Compare that preview with the QPU results. If the simulated improvement and the hardware improvement are similar, local simulation is a useful way to evaluate mitigation settings for this workload before you spend QPU time on them.\n"
msgstr "Sa Step 3.4, gumamit ka ng lokal na simulation para i-preview kung gaano mapapabuti ng PEC at TREX ang mga resulta. Ihambing ang preview na iyon sa mga resulta ng QPU. Kung magkatulad ang pagbuti sa simulation at sa hardware, kapaki-pakinabang na paraan ang lokal na simulation para suriin ang mga mitigation setting para sa workload na ito bago ka gumastos ng oras ng QPU para sa mga iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The comparison is approximate, for two reasons:\n"
msgstr "Tinatayang paghahambing lang ito, sa dalawang dahilan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simulations run the Cliffordized circuit from Step 3.1, while the hardware jobs run the original circuit.\n"
msgstr "Pinapatakbo ng mga simulation ang Cliffordized na circuit mula sa Step 3.1, habang pinapatakbo ng mga hardware job ang orihinal na circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simulations use the noise model learned in Step 3.3, while the mitigated hardware job uses the noise model that was refreshed in Step 4.2.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng mga simulation ang noise model na natutunan sa Step 3.3, habang ginagamit ng mitigated na hardware job ang noise model na na-refresh sa Step 4.2.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a direct check of the noise model itself, use the comparison of the Clifford circuit results in Step 3.4.4.\n"
msgstr "Para sa direktang pagsusuri sa mismong noise model, gamitin ang paghahambing ng mga resulta ng Clifford circuit sa Step 3.4.4.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/profiling-tools/extracted-outputs/3b67439e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/profiling-tools/extracted-outputs/3b67439e-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this run, mitigation reduced the mean absolute deviation from 0.290 to 0.046 in the simulation (about a factor of six) and from 0.202 to 0.050 on the QPU (about a factor of four). In both cases, the mitigated values scatter around 1, and most of them agree with 1 within their error bars.\n"
msgstr "Sa takbo na ito, binawasan ng mitigation ang mean absolute deviation mula 0.290 hanggang 0.046 sa simulation (humigit-kumulang anim na beses) at mula 0.202 hanggang 0.050 sa QPU (humigit-kumulang apat na beses). Sa parehong kaso, nagkakalat sa paligid ng 1 ang mga mitigated na value, at karamihan sa mga ito ay tumutugma sa 1 sa loob ng kanilang mga error bar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.4 Inspect execution spans {#44-inspect-execution-spans}"
msgstr "4.4 Suriin ang mga execution span {#44-inspect-execution-spans}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you submit circuits with multiple configurations, such as with gate twirling, IBM Quantum Compute Service does not necessarily run all circuit configurations at the same time. Instead, it groups them into chunks and runs one chunk per shot loop. A shot loop is a single round of execution on the quantum hardware, in which every circuit in the chunk is run for the requested number of shots.\n"
msgstr "Kapag nagsumite ka ng mga circuit na may maraming configuration, gaya ng may gate twirling, hindi kinakailangang patakbuhin ng IBM Quantum Compute Service ang lahat ng configuration ng circuit nang sabay-sabay. Sa halip, pinagsasama-sama nito ang mga ito sa mga chunk at nagpapatakbo ng isang chunk bawat shot loop. Ang shot loop ay isang round ng execution sa quantum hardware, kung saan pinapatakbo ang bawat circuit sa chunk para sa hiniling na bilang ng mga shot.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All jobs that are submitted to a real QPU require some classical pre-processing, such as translation into pulses that can be sent to the hardware. Because this pre-processing can be done in parallel, the service dequeues and starts multiple jobs at a time. The QPU, however, can process only one unit of work at a time. Therefore, if your job generates multiple chunks, they might be interleaved with the chunks of other users' jobs, and each chunk might have to wait for its turn on the QPU.\n"
msgstr "Ang lahat ng job na isinumite sa totoong QPU ay nangangailangan ng ilang classical na pre-processing, gaya ng pag-translate sa mga pulse na maipapadala sa hardware. Dahil maaaring gawin nang parallel ang pre-processing na ito, nagde-dequeue at nagsisimula ang service ng maraming job nang sabay. Gayunpaman, isang unit lang ng trabaho ang kayang iproseso ng QPU sa bawat pagkakataon. Kaya, kung bumubuo ng maraming chunk ang job mo, maaaring maghalo-halo ang mga ito sa mga chunk ng job ng ibang user, at maaaring kailangang maghintay ng bawat chunk ng turn nito sa QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The job result metadata reports the QPU execution timing for each chunk. The following visualization shows whether there are significant gaps between the executions of the chunks in your job. If the gaps are wider than your experiment can tolerate, you might want to rerun the job, or use [session execution mode](/guides/execution-modes#session-mode), which gives your workload exclusive access to the QPU.\n"
msgstr "Iniuulat ng metadata ng result ng job ang QPU execution timing para sa bawat chunk. Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na visualization kung may malalaking puwang sa pagitan ng mga execution ng mga chunk sa job mo. Kung mas malapad ang mga puwang kaysa sa kayang tiisin ng experiment mo, maaaring gusto mong patakbuhin ulit ang job, o gamitin ang [session execution mode](/guides/execution-modes#session-mode), na nagbibigay sa workload mo ng eksklusibong access sa QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Refer to [View execution spans](/guides/sampler-input-output#view-execution-spans) for more information.\n"
msgstr "Tingnan ang [View execution spans](/guides/sampler-input-output#view-execution-spans) para sa karagdagang impormasyon.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Chunk execution timeline for the mitigated job, showing two chunks and the gap between them](/docs/images/tutorials/profiling-tools/chunk-timing.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Chunk execution timeline for the mitigated job, showing two chunks and the gap between them](/docs/images/tutorials/profiling-tools/chunk-timing.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- Rerun the experiment with and without the `slow_gates_ac` calibration (Step 2.1), the refreshed device properties (Step 2.2), or session calibration (Step 4.1) to measure how much each tool improves the results for your workload.\n"
"- Try a cheaper error mitigation method such as zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE), and use local simulation and dry-run usage estimates to compare its cost and accuracy with those of PEC. The [`select-error-mitigation`](https://github.com/Qiskit/skills) AI agent skill can help you make this choice.\n"
"- Explore the full characterization suite, including randomized benchmarking, in the [Refresh backend properties with real-time benchmarking](/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking) tutorial.\n"
"- Learn more about the client-side primitives and the Executor in [Migrate from server-side to client-side Sampler and Estimator](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives).\n"
"- Apply these tools to your own experiments. Start with the tools that address your largest source of uncertainty, such as device quality, noise, cost, or execution timing.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Mga rekomendasyon\">\n"
"- Patakbuhin ulit ang experiment nang mayroon at walang `slow_gates_ac` calibration (Step 2.1), ang na-refresh na mga property ng device (Step 2.2), o session calibration (Step 4.1) para masukat kung gaano pinapabuti ng bawat tool ang mga resulta para sa workload mo.\n"
"- Subukan ang mas murang error mitigation method gaya ng zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE), at gumamit ng lokal na simulation at mga dry-run usage estimate para ihambing ang gastos at katumpakan nito sa PEC. Makakatulong sa pagpili ang [`select-error-mitigation`](https://github.com/Qiskit/skills) AI agent skill.\n"
"- I-explore ang buong characterization suite, kasama ang randomized benchmarking, sa tutorial na [Refresh backend properties with real-time benchmarking](/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking).\n"
"- Alamin pa ang tungkol sa mga client-side primitive at sa Executor sa [Migrate from server-side to client-side Sampler and Estimator](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives).\n"
"- I-apply ang mga tool na ito sa sarili mong mga experiment. Magsimula sa mga tool na tumutugon sa pinakamalaki mong pinagmumulan ng uncertainty, gaya ng kalidad ng device, noise, gastos, o execution timing.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

